<section class="section wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
  <h1>Take the system apart. Improve one piece at a time.</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="max-width: 680px;">
    I'm an AI product leader with a PhD in Systems Engineering. I break a complex system into its
    parts, work out how they interact, and improve one component at a time, so that it performs and
    so that a person can use it. For twenty years I've pointed that at one question: how do you deploy
    a system that decides things on a person's behalf, somewhere being wrong is expensive, and get
    people to trust it enough to actually use it?
  </p>
  <div style="margin-top: 1.75rem;">
    <span class="tag tag-neutral" style="margin-right: 0.5rem;">Human-AI Interaction</span>
    <span class="tag tag-neutral" style="margin-right: 0.5rem;">AI Governance</span>
    <span class="tag tag-neutral">Systems Engineering</span>
  </div>
</section>

