  <div class="timeline">
    <div class="timeline__item">
      <div class="timeline__period">2009 to 2013</div>
      <h3 class="timeline__role">Product Manager, Blackboard</h3>
      <p>Started my career proving UX moves revenue. Shipped 84 mobile apps, drove a 64% year-over-year
      jump in sales, and helped build the case that led to the company's acquisition.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline__item">
      <div class="timeline__period">2012 to 2017</div>
      <h3 class="timeline__role">PhD Researcher, Virginia Tech, alongside IBM and Amazon/Sonos</h3>
      <p>Pursued a PhD in Industrial &amp; Systems Engineering while running full industry roles at the
      same time: Product Manager at IBM (hired as a User Experience Engineer), scaling SaaS adoption
      75x, then UX research for Amazon Echo and Sonos Play:5. The dissertation asked what a system
      should surface to a person under load, when it should defer, and how it should fail safely.
      Selected as an NSF I-Corps Graduate Fellow.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline__item">
      <div class="timeline__period">2014 to 2017</div>
      <h3 class="timeline__role">Founder and Principal, Product, Redfearn Group</h3>
      <p>Another concurrent thread during the PhD years: TALOS, U.S. Special Operations Command's
      powered exoskeleton program. Defined the human-AI interaction model for the system, secured $750K
      in research funding across two federal R&amp;D programs, and shipped two prototypes on time and
      under budget.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline__item">
      <div class="timeline__period">2018 to 2020</div>
      <h3 class="timeline__role">Lab Director &amp; Visiting Assistant Professor, Brigham Young University</h3>
      <p>Built the Advanced HCI curriculum around intelligent and adaptive interfaces: how people direct,
      correct, and override systems that decide for them. Founded a university innovation lab from zero,
      raised $325K, and mentored 200+ students.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline__item">
      <div class="timeline__period">2018 to 2024</div>
      <h3 class="timeline__role">Senior Technical Product Manager, Defense Technology Contractor</h3>
      <p>Owned a $45M portfolio across up to 14 concurrent programs, leading an org of 12 across five
      teams. Led applied LLM research at the Army Cyber Institute at West Point, including two published
      assessments of adversarial AI risk in critical infrastructure. Shipped a 0-to-1 procurement
      platform that billions in contract value flowed through, and helped launch a commercial AI/ML
      platform searching 400M+ documents.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline__item">
      <div class="timeline__period">2024 to 2026</div>
      <h3 class="timeline__role">Founder and Principal, AI Product, Redfearn Group</h3>
      <p>Led AI strategy and governance for Next Generation 9-1-1: where AI can be safely deployed in a
      call center where a wrong output costs a life. The assessments drove pilot and procurement
      decisions and fed national guidance on AI adoption in emergency communication centers.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline__item">
      <div class="timeline__period">2026 to Present</div>
      <h3 class="timeline__role">Senior Solutions Strategist (Enterprise AI Platform Product Management), Large Public Institution</h3>
      <p>Architected the product spec for an enterprise AI platform serving more than 200,000 learners,
      and scaled from one program to four. I prototype in working software, building daily with Claude
      Code, so architecture decisions are tested against something running before they reach a
      document.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--border-top wrap">
  <h2 class="section-label">How I Work</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Bridge, don't translate</h3>
      <p class="small">I don't translate between engineering and the business. I sit in both rooms
      well enough that translation isn't necessary.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Governance as infrastructure</h3>
      <p class="small">Compliance and ethics review, built into the pipeline from day one. It ships
      faster than bolting it on after legal finds the problem.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Numbers over opinions</h3>
      <p class="small">If a decision can be modeled, it should be. Multi-criteria frameworks beat
      whoever presents last in the room.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="small" style="margin-top: 2rem;"><a href="/frameworks/" class="btn btn-ghost">See these applied in practice &rarr;</a></p>
</section>

